        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Getting started with streamlit\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## How to create and run a Streamlit app\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Install Streamlit.\n",
        "\n",
        "   ```bash\n",
        "   pip install streamlit\n",
        "   ```\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"height: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Create a Python script (e.g., `app.py`).\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"height: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Import Streamlit at the top of your script:\n",
        "\n",
        "   ```python\n",
        "   import streamlit as st\n",
        "   ```\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"height: 10px;\"></div>\n",
        "\n",
        "4. Run your app from the terminal:\n",
        "\n",
        "   ```bash\n",
        "   streamlit run app.py\n",
        "   ```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## What can we put in a Streamlit app?\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's start with text: a title, a header and a subheader.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "`app.py`:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.title(\"This is a title\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.header(\"This is a header\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"This is a subheader\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "App:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.title(\"This is a title\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.header(\"This is a header\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"This is a subheader\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Other Streamlit text\n",
        "\n",
        "Dedicated commands for different text styles, or `st.write()` for general-purpose output.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(\"Text\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.markdown(\"Text with **markdown**\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.text(\"Text **without markdown**\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.badge(\"Badge\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.caption(\"Caption\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.code(\"Code\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(\"Text\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.markdown(\"Text with **markdown**\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.text(\"Text **without markdown**\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.badge(\"Badge\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.caption(\"Caption\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.code(\"Code\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Widgets: `st.radio`\n",
        "\n",
        "Widgets are interactive controls that let users provide input.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, `st.radio` lets users choose one option from a list.\n",
        "\n",
        "Set the prompt with `label`, the choices with `options`, and the starting position with `index` (`0` selects the first option).\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    default=\"A\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    default=\"A\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Widgets: `st.pills` and `st.segmented_control`\n",
        "\n",
        "These display the choices as buttons rather than a radio list.\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `label` and `options` as before, but set the starting choice with `default` (e.g., `\"A\"`) rather than its position.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.segmented_control(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    default=\"A\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.radio(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    index=0,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.segmented_control(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    default=\"A\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.radio(\n",
        "    label=\"Choose an option\",\n",
        "    options=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"],\n",
        "    index=0,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Widgets: `st.slider` and `st.numeric_input`\n",
        "\n",
        "Drag a slider or type a number to set a numeric value.\n",
        "\n",
        "Set the prompt with `label`, the limits with `min_value` and `max_value`, the starting value with `value`, and the increment with `step`.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\",\n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\",\n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Accessing the chosen value\n",
        "\n",
        "Access the chosen value through a variable or `st.session_state`.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "To assign the widget's return value to a variable:\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"3,11\"}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "chosen_value = st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(f\"Chosen number: {chosen_value}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "chosen_value = st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(f\"Chosen number: {chosen_value}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Accessing the chosen value\n",
        "\n",
        "Alternatively, give the widget a `key` to access its value through `st.session_state`.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"9,12\"}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1,\n",
        "    key=\"chosen_value\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(f\"Chosen number: {st.session_state.chosen_value}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Pick a number\", \n",
        "    min_value=0,\n",
        "    max_value=10,\n",
        "    value=2,\n",
        "    step=1,\n",
        "    key=\"chosen_value\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.write(f\"Chosen number: {st.session_state.chosen_value}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Session state\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Session state keeps track of values between script re-runs, like a dictionary for the current user's session.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "For our slider with a `key`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. The user chooses a new inter-arrival time.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Streamlit updates the value in `st.session_state`.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. The script reruns, reading and using the updated value.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "![](gif/session_state_.gif)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Let's build a streamlit app for our DES model\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Let's build a streamlit app!\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll use the DES model from session 2C. As a reminder:\n",
        "\n",
        "* It has `Param`, `Patient`, `Model`, and `Trial` classes.\n",
        "* It simulates a simple nurse clinic.\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/model_diagram.drawio.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Before we build the app...\n",
        "\n",
        "This app will help decision-makers explore staffing options, considering both patient waiting times and staffing costs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let’s add an hourly cost per nurse.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"10,18\"}\n",
        "class Param:\n",
        "    def __init__(\n",
        "        self,\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=5,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=6,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=1,\n",
        "        num_nurses=1,\n",
        "        sim_duration=120,\n",
        "        num_replications=5,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=30,\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        self.mean_patient_inter = mean_patient_inter\n",
        "        self.mean_nurse_consult_time = mean_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.sd_nurse_consult_time = sd_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.num_nurses = num_nurses\n",
        "        self.sim_duration = sim_duration\n",
        "        self.num_replications = num_replications\n",
        "        self.nurse_cost_per_hour = nurse_cost_per_hour\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Before we build the app...\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculate the total staffing cost from the number of nurses, the simulation duration and the hourly rate.\n",
        "\n",
        "This lets us compare the cost of each staffing option alongside its effect on waiting times.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"9-14\"}\n",
        "        self.ci_lower_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse - (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.ci_upper_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse + (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.total_nurse_cost = (\n",
        "            self.param.num_nurses\n",
        "            * self.param.sim_duration\n",
        "            / 60\n",
        "            * self.param.nurse_cost_per_hour\n",
        "        )\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Updated model with nurse costs\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-overflow=\"scroll\" code-line-numbers=\"29,37,146-152\"}\n",
        "import math\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import simpy\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "\n",
        "# stlite requires imports without dotted names\n",
        "from sim_tools import distributions\n",
        "Exponential = distributions.Exponential\n",
        "Lognormal = distributions.Lognormal\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Patient:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, p_id):\n",
        "        self.id = p_id\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Param:\n",
        "    def __init__(\n",
        "        self,\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=5,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=6,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=1,\n",
        "        num_nurses=1,\n",
        "        sim_duration=120,\n",
        "        num_replications=5,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=30,  # NEW\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        self.mean_patient_inter = mean_patient_inter\n",
        "        self.mean_nurse_consult_time = mean_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.sd_nurse_consult_time = sd_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.num_nurses = num_nurses\n",
        "        self.sim_duration = sim_duration\n",
        "        self.num_replications = num_replications\n",
        "        self.nurse_cost_per_hour = nurse_cost_per_hour  # NEW\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Model:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param, replication_id):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.replication_id = replication_id\n",
        "        self.env = simpy.Environment()\n",
        "        self.patient_counter = 0\n",
        "        self.nurse = simpy.Resource(self.env, capacity=self.param.num_nurses)\n",
        "\n",
        "        ss = np.random.SeedSequence(self.replication_id)\n",
        "        seeds = ss.spawn(2)\n",
        "        self.patient_inter_dist = Exponential(\n",
        "            mean=self.param.mean_patient_inter, random_seed=seeds[0]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        self.nurse_consult_time_dist = Lognormal(\n",
        "            mean=self.param.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "            stdev=self.param.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "            random_seed=seeds[1],\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.list_of_patients = []\n",
        "        self.mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "    def generator_patient_arrivals(self):\n",
        "        while True:\n",
        "            self.patient_counter += 1\n",
        "            p = Patient(self.patient_counter)\n",
        "            self.list_of_patients.append(p)\n",
        "            self.env.process(self.attend_clinic(p))\n",
        "            sampled_inter = self.patient_inter_dist.sample()\n",
        "            yield self.env.timeout(sampled_inter)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def attend_clinic(self, patient):\n",
        "        start_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "\n",
        "        with self.nurse.request() as req:\n",
        "            yield req\n",
        "            end_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "            patient.q_time_nurse = end_q_nurse - start_q_nurse\n",
        "            sampled_nurse_act_time = self.nurse_consult_time_dist.sample()\n",
        "            yield self.env.timeout(sampled_nurse_act_time)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def run_model(self):\n",
        "        self.env.process(self.generator_patient_arrivals())\n",
        "        self.env.run(until=self.param.sim_duration)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(self, entity_list):\n",
        "        entity_dateframe = pd.DataFrame(entity.__dict__ for entity in entity_list)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return entity_dateframe\n",
        "\n",
        "    def calculate_run_results(self, entity_dataframe):\n",
        "        self.mean_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].mean()\n",
        "        self.sd_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].std()\n",
        "        self.perc_90_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].quantile(0.9)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Trial:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.list_of_simulation_replications = []\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.ci_lower_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.ci_upper_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.se_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "    def run_trial(self):\n",
        "        for replication_id in range(self.param.num_replications):\n",
        "            model_replication = Model(self.param, replication_id)\n",
        "            model_replication.run_model()\n",
        "            patient_df = model_replication.convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(\n",
        "                model_replication.list_of_patients\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            model_replication.calculate_run_results(patient_df)\n",
        "            self.list_of_simulation_replications.append(model_replication)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def calculate_trial_results(self):\n",
        "        self.replication_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "            replication.__dict__ for replication in self.list_of_simulation_replications\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].std()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\n",
        "            \"mean_q_time_nurse\"\n",
        "        ].quantile(0.9)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.se_q_time_nurse = self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse / math.sqrt(\n",
        "            self.param.num_replications\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        t = stats.t.ppf(0.975, df=self.param.num_replications - 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.ci_lower_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse - (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.ci_upper_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse + (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        # NEW\n",
        "        self.total_nurse_cost = (\n",
        "            self.param.num_nurses\n",
        "            * self.param.sim_duration\n",
        "            / 60\n",
        "            * self.param.nurse_cost_per_hour\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "base_case_params = Param()\n",
        "base_case_trial = Trial(base_case_params)\n",
        "base_case_trial.run_trial()\n",
        "base_case_trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "print (\"BASE CASE TRIAL RESULTS\")\n",
        "print (\"-----------------------\")\n",
        "print (\"Queuing Time for the Nurse\")\n",
        "print (f\"Mean : {base_case_trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"SD : {base_case_trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"90th Perc : {base_case_trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"Standard Error : {base_case_trial.se_q_time_nurse:.2f}\")\n",
        "print (\n",
        "    f\"95% CI : ({base_case_trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse:.2f}, \",\n",
        "    f\"{base_case_trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse:.2f}) minutes\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "print ()\n",
        "\n",
        "what_if_params = Param(num_nurses=2)\n",
        "what_if_trial = Trial(what_if_params)\n",
        "what_if_trial.run_trial()\n",
        "what_if_trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "print (\"2 NURSES TRIAL RESULTS\")\n",
        "print (\"----------------------\")\n",
        "print (\"Queuing Time for the Nurse\")\n",
        "print (f\"Mean : {what_if_trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"SD : {what_if_trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"90th Perc : {what_if_trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"Standard Error : {what_if_trial.se_q_time_nurse:.2f}\")\n",
        "print (\n",
        "    f\"95% CI : ({what_if_trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse:.2f}, \",\n",
        "    f\"{what_if_trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse:.2f}) minutes\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "print ()\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Streamlit app\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll build a simple app in four steps:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Create the app **script**.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Get **inputs** from the user.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Run** the model using those inputs.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Display** the results.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Create the app script\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Create `app.py` in the same folder as `model.py`.\n",
        "\n",
        "It should contain these imports:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "import plotly.express as px\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "from model import Param, Trial\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "* `plotly.express`: chart the results.\n",
        "* `streamlit`: build the interface.\n",
        "* `Param` and `Trial`: configure and run the model. Here, `model` refers to `model.py` in the same folder. The import makes `Param` and `Trial` available in our app.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"10%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment}\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Why two Python files?**\n",
        ">\n",
        "> * Run and test the model independently of the app.\n",
        "> * Avoid redefining model classes each time Streamlit reruns.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Get inputs from the user\n",
        "\n",
        "**Which model parameters should users be able to change?**  \n",
        "For this app, we'll include all everything in `Param`.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "class Param:\n",
        "    def __init__(\n",
        "        self,\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=5,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=6,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=1,\n",
        "        num_nurses=1,\n",
        "        sim_duration=120,\n",
        "        num_replications=5,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=30,\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        self.mean_patient_inter = mean_patient_inter\n",
        "        self.mean_nurse_consult_time = mean_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.sd_nurse_consult_time = sd_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.num_nurses = num_nurses\n",
        "        self.sim_duration = sim_duration\n",
        "        self.num_replications = num_replications\n",
        "        self.nurse_cost_per_hour = nurse_cost_per_hour\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "* Mean time between arrivals\n",
        "* Mean and SD of consultation time\n",
        "* Number of nurses\n",
        "* Simulation duration\n",
        "* Number of replications\n",
        "* Hourly cost per nurse\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inputs: inter-arrival time\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll use our original default (`5`), then choose some suitable limits and a step size.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=7.0,\n",
        "    value=5.0,\n",
        "    step=0.25,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=7.0,\n",
        "    value=5.0,\n",
        "    step=0.25,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inputs: Consultation time\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=9.0,\n",
        "    value=6.0,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=9.0,\n",
        "    value=6.0,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inputs: Number of nurses\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.pills(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of nurses\",\n",
        "    options=range(1, 5),\n",
        "    default=1,\n",
        "    key=\"num_nurses\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of nurses\",\n",
        "    options=range(1, 5),\n",
        "    default=1,\n",
        "    key=\"num_nurses\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inputs: Hourly cost\n",
        "\n",
        "All widgets have a `help` parameter.\n",
        "\n",
        "We can use it here to explain what the hourly cost should include.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=30.0,\n",
        "    step=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "    help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=30.0,\n",
        "    step=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "    help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inputs: Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=50,\n",
        "    max_value=200,\n",
        "    value=120,\n",
        "    key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "    min_value=10,\n",
        "    max_value=50,\n",
        "    value=30,\n",
        "    key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=50,\n",
        "    max_value=200,\n",
        "    value=120,\n",
        "    key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "    min_value=10,\n",
        "    max_value=50,\n",
        "    value=30,\n",
        "    key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Complete set of user inputs for the app\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"55%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Patients\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=7.0,\n",
        "    value=5.0,\n",
        "    step=0.25,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=9.0,\n",
        "    value=6.0,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(label=\"Number of nurses\", options=range(1, 5), default=1, key=\"num_nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=30.0,\n",
        "    step=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "    help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.space(size=\"xxsmall\")\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Simulation\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=50,\n",
        "    max_value=200,\n",
        "    value=120,\n",
        "    key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "    min_value=10,\n",
        "    max_value=50,\n",
        "    value=30,\n",
        "    key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"45%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"height: 550px;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Patients\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=7.0,\n",
        "    value=5.0,\n",
        "    step=0.25,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=9.0,\n",
        "    value=6.0,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(label=\"Number of nurses\", options=range(1, 5), default=1, key=\"num_nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=30.0,\n",
        "    step=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "    help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.space(size=\"xxsmall\")\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Simulation\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=50,\n",
        "    max_value=200,\n",
        "    value=120,\n",
        "    key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "    min_value=10,\n",
        "    max_value=50,\n",
        "    value=30,\n",
        "    key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Run model using the inputs\n",
        "\n",
        "Now we want to run the model in our app, using the selected values instead of relying on the model's defaults.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "params = Param(\n",
        "    mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "    mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "    sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "    num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "    sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "    num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "    nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        ")\n",
        "trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "trial.run_trial()\n",
        "trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## When should the model run?\n",
        "\n",
        "Changing an input reruns the script, but we only want to run the simulation when the user is ready.\n",
        "\n",
        "`st.button()` adds a button. Clicking it re-runs the script and returns `True` for that run, so the indented simulation code executes.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"1\"}\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Displaying simulation results\n",
        "\n",
        "Previously we printed results to the terminal. We can display similar text in our app.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"15-37\"}\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "    results = {\n",
        "        \"mean\": trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"sd\": trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"p90\": trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"se\": trial.se_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"cost\": trial.total_nurse_cost,\n",
        "        \"df\": trial.replication_df,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Scenario summary\")\n",
        "    st.write(f\"\"\"\n",
        "    Summary of nurse queue times across **all** replications.\n",
        "\n",
        "    * Mean: {results[\"mean\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * SD: {results[\"sd\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * 90th Perc: {results[\"p90\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * Standard error: {results[\"se\"]:.2f}\n",
        "    * 95% CI: ({results[\"ci_lower\"]:.2f}, {results[\"ci_upper\"]:.2f}) minutes\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Total nurse staffing cost: £{results[\"cost\"]:,.2f}\n",
        "    \"\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Charts\n",
        "\n",
        "Various plotting libraries are supported. For example, using plotly, you create a figure then use `st.plotly_chart()` to display it in the app.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"39-50\"}\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "    results = {\n",
        "        \"mean\": trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"sd\": trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"p90\": trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"se\": trial.se_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"cost\": trial.total_nurse_cost,\n",
        "        \"df\": trial.replication_df,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Scenario summary\")\n",
        "    st.write(f\"\"\"\n",
        "    Summary of nurse queue times across **all** replications.\n",
        "\n",
        "    * Mean: {results[\"mean\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * SD: {results[\"sd\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * 90th Perc: {results[\"p90\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * Standard error: {results[\"se\"]:.2f}\n",
        "    * 95% CI: ({results[\"ci_lower\"]:.2f}, {results[\"ci_upper\"]:.2f}) minutes\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Total nurse staffing cost: £{results[\"cost\"]:,.2f}\n",
        "    \"\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Results from individual replications\")\n",
        "    st.write(\n",
        "        \"The chart shows how the mean nurse queue time varies between **individual** replications.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig = px.histogram(\n",
        "        data_frame=results[\"df\"],\n",
        "        x=\"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "        labels={\"mean_q_time_nurse\": \"Mean nurse queue time\"},\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    fig.update_layout(yaxis_title=\"Number of replications\")\n",
        "    st.plotly_chart(fig)\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dataframes\n",
        "\n",
        "We can create interactive tables with `st.dataframe()` or static tables with `st.table()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"52-62\"}\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "    results = {\n",
        "        \"mean\": trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"sd\": trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"p90\": trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"se\": trial.se_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"cost\": trial.total_nurse_cost,\n",
        "        \"df\": trial.replication_df,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Scenario summary\")\n",
        "    st.write(f\"\"\"\n",
        "    Summary of nurse queue times across **all** replications.\n",
        "\n",
        "    * Mean: {results[\"mean\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * SD: {results[\"sd\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * 90th Perc: {results[\"p90\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * Standard error: {results[\"se\"]:.2f}\n",
        "    * 95% CI: ({results[\"ci_lower\"]:.2f}, {results[\"ci_upper\"]:.2f}) minutes\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Total nurse staffing cost: £{results[\"cost\"]:,.2f}\n",
        "    \"\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Results from individual replications\")\n",
        "    st.write(\n",
        "        \"The chart shows how the mean nurse queue time varies between **individual** replications.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig = px.histogram(\n",
        "        data_frame=results[\"df\"],\n",
        "        x=\"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "        labels={\"mean_q_time_nurse\": \"Mean nurse queue time\"},\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    fig.update_layout(yaxis_title=\"Number of replications\")\n",
        "    st.plotly_chart(fig)\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.dataframe(\n",
        "        results[\"df\"][\n",
        "            [\n",
        "                \"replication_id\",\n",
        "                \"patient_counter\",\n",
        "                \"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                \"sd_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                \"perc_90_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Our app\n",
        "\n",
        "```{stlite-python}\n",
        "# stlite requires micropip and installation without dotted module names\n",
        "import micropip\n",
        "await micropip.install(\"plotly\")\n",
        "await micropip.install(\"sim-tools\")\n",
        "await micropip.install(\"simpy\")\n",
        "\n",
        "import streamlit as st\n",
        "from plotly import express as px\n",
        "\n",
        "import math\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import simpy\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "\n",
        "# stlite requires imports without dotted names\n",
        "from sim_tools import distributions\n",
        "Exponential = distributions.Exponential\n",
        "Lognormal = distributions.Lognormal\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Patient:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, p_id):\n",
        "        self.id = p_id\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Param:\n",
        "    def __init__(\n",
        "        self,\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=5,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=6,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=1,\n",
        "        num_nurses=1,\n",
        "        sim_duration=120,\n",
        "        num_replications=5,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=30,  # NEW\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        self.mean_patient_inter = mean_patient_inter\n",
        "        self.mean_nurse_consult_time = mean_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.sd_nurse_consult_time = sd_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "        self.num_nurses = num_nurses\n",
        "        self.sim_duration = sim_duration\n",
        "        self.num_replications = num_replications\n",
        "        self.nurse_cost_per_hour = nurse_cost_per_hour  # NEW\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Model:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param, replication_id):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.replication_id = replication_id\n",
        "        self.env = simpy.Environment()\n",
        "        self.patient_counter = 0\n",
        "        self.nurse = simpy.Resource(self.env, capacity=self.param.num_nurses)\n",
        "\n",
        "        ss = np.random.SeedSequence(self.replication_id)\n",
        "        seeds = ss.spawn(2)\n",
        "        self.patient_inter_dist = Exponential(\n",
        "            mean=self.param.mean_patient_inter, random_seed=seeds[0]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        self.nurse_consult_time_dist = Lognormal(\n",
        "            mean=self.param.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "            stdev=self.param.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "            random_seed=seeds[1],\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.list_of_patients = []\n",
        "        self.mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "    def generator_patient_arrivals(self):\n",
        "        while True:\n",
        "            self.patient_counter += 1\n",
        "            p = Patient(self.patient_counter)\n",
        "            self.list_of_patients.append(p)\n",
        "            self.env.process(self.attend_clinic(p))\n",
        "            sampled_inter = self.patient_inter_dist.sample()\n",
        "            yield self.env.timeout(sampled_inter)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def attend_clinic(self, patient):\n",
        "        start_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "\n",
        "        with self.nurse.request() as req:\n",
        "            yield req\n",
        "            end_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "            patient.q_time_nurse = end_q_nurse - start_q_nurse\n",
        "            sampled_nurse_act_time = self.nurse_consult_time_dist.sample()\n",
        "            yield self.env.timeout(sampled_nurse_act_time)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def run_model(self):\n",
        "        self.env.process(self.generator_patient_arrivals())\n",
        "        self.env.run(until=self.param.sim_duration)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(self, entity_list):\n",
        "        entity_dateframe = pd.DataFrame(entity.__dict__ for entity in entity_list)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return entity_dateframe\n",
        "\n",
        "    def calculate_run_results(self, entity_dataframe):\n",
        "        self.mean_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].mean()\n",
        "        self.sd_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].std()\n",
        "        self.perc_90_q_time_nurse = entity_dataframe[\"q_time_nurse\"].quantile(0.9)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Trial:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.list_of_simulation_replications = []\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.ci_lower_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.ci_upper_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.se_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "    def run_trial(self):\n",
        "        for replication_id in range(self.param.num_replications):\n",
        "            model_replication = Model(self.param, replication_id)\n",
        "            model_replication.run_model()\n",
        "            patient_df = model_replication.convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(\n",
        "                model_replication.list_of_patients\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            model_replication.calculate_run_results(patient_df)\n",
        "            self.list_of_simulation_replications.append(model_replication)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def calculate_trial_results(self):\n",
        "        self.replication_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "            replication.__dict__ for replication in self.list_of_simulation_replications\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].std()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\n",
        "            \"mean_q_time_nurse\"\n",
        "        ].quantile(0.9)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.se_q_time_nurse = self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse / math.sqrt(\n",
        "            self.param.num_replications\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        t = stats.t.ppf(0.975, df=self.param.num_replications - 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.ci_lower_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse - (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.ci_upper_q_time_nurse = self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse + (\n",
        "            t * self.se_q_time_nurse\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        # NEW\n",
        "        self.total_nurse_cost = (\n",
        "            self.param.num_nurses\n",
        "            * self.param.sim_duration\n",
        "            / 60\n",
        "            * self.param.nurse_cost_per_hour\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "base_case_params = Param()\n",
        "base_case_trial = Trial(base_case_params)\n",
        "base_case_trial.run_trial()\n",
        "base_case_trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "print (\"BASE CASE TRIAL RESULTS\")\n",
        "print (\"-----------------------\")\n",
        "print (\"Queuing Time for the Nurse\")\n",
        "print (f\"Mean : {base_case_trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"SD : {base_case_trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"90th Perc : {base_case_trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"Standard Error : {base_case_trial.se_q_time_nurse:.2f}\")\n",
        "print (\n",
        "    f\"95% CI : ({base_case_trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse:.2f}, \",\n",
        "    f\"{base_case_trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse:.2f}) minutes\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "print ()\n",
        "\n",
        "what_if_params = Param(num_nurses=2)\n",
        "what_if_trial = Trial(what_if_params)\n",
        "what_if_trial.run_trial()\n",
        "what_if_trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "print (\"2 NURSES TRIAL RESULTS\")\n",
        "print (\"----------------------\")\n",
        "print (\"Queuing Time for the Nurse\")\n",
        "print (f\"Mean : {what_if_trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"SD : {what_if_trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"90th Perc : {what_if_trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse:.2f} minutes\")\n",
        "print (f\"Standard Error : {what_if_trial.se_q_time_nurse:.2f}\")\n",
        "print (\n",
        "    f\"95% CI : ({what_if_trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse:.2f}, \",\n",
        "    f\"{what_if_trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse:.2f}) minutes\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "print ()\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Patients\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=7.0,\n",
        "    value=5.0,\n",
        "    step=0.25,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=3.0,\n",
        "    max_value=9.0,\n",
        "    value=6.0,\n",
        "    key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.pills(label=\"Number of nurses\", options=range(1, 5), default=1, key=\"num_nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.number_input(\n",
        "    label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "    min_value=0.0,\n",
        "    value=30.0,\n",
        "    step=1.0,\n",
        "    key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "    help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.space(size=\"xxsmall\")\n",
        "st.subheader(\"Simulation\")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "    min_value=50,\n",
        "    max_value=200,\n",
        "    value=120,\n",
        "    key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "st.slider(\n",
        "    label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "    min_value=10,\n",
        "    max_value=50,\n",
        "    value=30,\n",
        "    key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "    results = {\n",
        "        \"mean\": trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"sd\": trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"p90\": trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"se\": trial.se_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"cost\": trial.total_nurse_cost,\n",
        "        \"df\": trial.replication_df,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Scenario summary\")\n",
        "    st.write(f\"\"\"\n",
        "    Summary of nurse queue times across **all** replications.\n",
        "\n",
        "    * Mean: {results[\"mean\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * SD: {results[\"sd\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * 90th Perc: {results[\"p90\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * Standard error: {results[\"se\"]:.2f}\n",
        "    * 95% CI: ({results[\"ci_lower\"]:.2f}, {results[\"ci_upper\"]:.2f}) minutes\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Total nurse staffing cost: £{results[\"cost\"]:,.2f}\n",
        "    \"\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Results from individual replications\")\n",
        "    st.write(\n",
        "        \"The chart shows how the mean nurse queue time varies between **individual** replications.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig = px.histogram(\n",
        "        data_frame=results[\"df\"],\n",
        "        x=\"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "        labels={\"mean_q_time_nurse\": \"Mean nurse queue time\"},\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    fig.update_layout(yaxis_title=\"Number of replications\")\n",
        "    st.plotly_chart(fig)\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.dataframe(\n",
        "        results[\"df\"][\n",
        "            [\n",
        "                \"replication_id\",\n",
        "                \"patient_counter\",\n",
        "                \"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                \"sd_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                \"perc_90_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Improving layout: `st.container`\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "We can group elements using `st.container()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's add a border around our model parameters using `with st.container(border=True):`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Indent the code for the elements you want inside the container.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"1\"}\n",
        "with st.container(border=True):\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Patients\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.slider(\n",
        "        label=\"Mean patient inter-arrival time (minutes)\",\n",
        "        min_value=3.0,\n",
        "        max_value=7.0,\n",
        "        value=5.0,\n",
        "        step=0.25,\n",
        "        key=\"mean_patient_inter\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.number_input(\n",
        "        label=\"Mean nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "        min_value=3.0,\n",
        "        max_value=9.0,\n",
        "        value=6.0,\n",
        "        key=\"mean_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.number_input(\n",
        "        label=\"Standard deviation of nurse consultation length (minutes)\",\n",
        "        min_value=0.0,\n",
        "        value=1.0,\n",
        "        key=\"sd_nurse_consult_time\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.pills(label=\"Number of nurses\", options=range(1, 5), default=1, key=\"num_nurses\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.number_input(\n",
        "        label=\"Cost per nurse per hour (£)\",\n",
        "        min_value=0.0,\n",
        "        value=30.0,\n",
        "        step=1.0,\n",
        "        key=\"nurse_cost_per_hour\",\n",
        "        help=\"Nurses are costed for the full simulation duration, including time when they are not seeing patients\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.space(size=\"xxsmall\")\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Simulation\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.slider(\n",
        "        label=\"Simulation duration (minutes)\",\n",
        "        min_value=50,\n",
        "        max_value=200,\n",
        "        value=120,\n",
        "        key=\"sim_duration\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.slider(\n",
        "        label=\"Number of replications\",\n",
        "        min_value=10,\n",
        "        max_value=50,\n",
        "        value=30,\n",
        "        key=\"num_replications\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Improving layout: `st.expander`\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "`st.expander()` can be used to hide optional data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's hide the dataframe with results from individual replications.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"70%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"52\"}\n",
        "if st.button(\"Run simulation\", type=\"primary\"):\n",
        "    params = Param(\n",
        "        mean_patient_inter=st.session_state.mean_patient_inter,\n",
        "        mean_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.mean_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        sd_nurse_consult_time=st.session_state.sd_nurse_consult_time,\n",
        "        num_nurses=st.session_state.num_nurses,\n",
        "        sim_duration=st.session_state.sim_duration,\n",
        "        num_replications=st.session_state.num_replications,\n",
        "        nurse_cost_per_hour=st.session_state.nurse_cost_per_hour,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    trial = Trial(param=params)\n",
        "    trial.run_trial()\n",
        "    trial.calculate_trial_results()\n",
        "\n",
        "    results = {\n",
        "        \"mean\": trial.trial_mean_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"sd\": trial.trial_sd_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"p90\": trial.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"se\": trial.se_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": trial.ci_lower_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": trial.ci_upper_q_time_nurse,\n",
        "        \"cost\": trial.total_nurse_cost,\n",
        "        \"df\": trial.replication_df,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Scenario summary\")\n",
        "    st.write(f\"\"\"\n",
        "    Summary of nurse queue times across **all** replications.\n",
        "\n",
        "    * Mean: {results[\"mean\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * SD: {results[\"sd\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * 90th Perc: {results[\"p90\"]:.2f} minutes.\n",
        "    * Standard error: {results[\"se\"]:.2f}\n",
        "    * 95% CI: ({results[\"ci_lower\"]:.2f}, {results[\"ci_upper\"]:.2f}) minutes\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Total nurse staffing cost: £{results[\"cost\"]:,.2f}\n",
        "    \"\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    st.subheader(\"Results from individual replications\")\n",
        "    st.write(\n",
        "        \"The chart shows how the mean nurse queue time varies between **individual** replications.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig = px.histogram(\n",
        "        data_frame=results[\"df\"],\n",
        "        x=\"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "        labels={\"mean_q_time_nurse\": \"Mean nurse queue time\"},\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    fig.update_layout(yaxis_title=\"Number of replications\")\n",
        "    st.plotly_chart(fig)\n",
        "\n",
        "    with st.expander(\"View underlying data from each replication\"):\n",
        "        st.dataframe(\n",
        "            results[\"df\"][\n",
        "                [\n",
        "                    \"replication_id\",\n",
        "                    \"patient_counter\",\n",
        "                    \"mean_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                    \"sd_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                    \"perc_90_q_time_nurse\",\n",
        "                ]\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Improving layout: `st.space`\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `st.space()` to add space between sections of the app.\n",
        "\n",
        "Set `size` to adjust the spacing. The default is `\"small\"`.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"70%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-numbers=\"47,91,105\"}\n",
